+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "  use: [agents({ agents: ['orderAgent', 'refundAgent'], maxDelegations: 3, historyLength: 4 })],\n});",
+  "cause": "The triage agent (the entry point for the support chat) was defined without a session `store`, so Genkit's agent runtime rejects any attempt to resume a chat via `sessionId`, forcing the customer to start a brand-new session and repeat the order number.",
+  "evidence": "Calling triage.chat({ sessionId }).send(...) a second time with the same sessionId throws `FAILED_PRECONDITION: Cannot use 'sessionId' with agent 'triage': this agent has no store configured (client-managed state). Send 'state' instead.` (from @genkit-ai/ai's assertInitMatchesStateManagement in agent.mjs); refundAgent, which does have `store` configured, has no such problem. Adding `store` (the same FileSessionStore already used by refundAgent) to the triage agent fixed it: a two-turn test session ('My order is A-1001.' then 'What is its status?', resumed only by sessionId) correctly answered 'Your order A-1001 is currently shipped.' on the second turn without repeating the order id."
+}
